# ============================================================
#  Erebus scope - caporia.co
#  Modeled on a HackerOne-style bug-bounty program scope.
#  Owner-authorized: the operator owns caporia.co and approves testing.
#
#  Load it:   erebus console --serve --scope scopes/caporia.co.scope
#             (or paste / upload it in the dashboard: Targets > Scope)
#  Format:    one target per line; IP, CIDR, hostname, or *.wildcard
#             '#' starts a comment. The file is an ALLOWLIST - anything
#             not listed is out of scope and will be refused.
# ============================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
#  IN SCOPE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Primary domain and every subdomain (wildcard = apex + any depth).
caporia.co
*.caporia.co

# Explicit service hosts (optional - the wildcard already covers these;
# uncomment if you later tighten the wildcard to specific hosts).
# www.caporia.co
# api.caporia.co
# app.caporia.co
# staging.caporia.co
# dev.caporia.co

# Owned lab / infrastructure (set these to your REAL ranges, then uncomment).
# 10.10.0.0/24          # home lab segment
# 192.168.56.0/24       # VM host-only network

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
#  OUT OF SCOPE   (documented here; the allowlist simply never allows them)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# - Any host not under caporia.co or the lab ranges above.
# - Third-party / managed platforms, even on a caporia.co CNAME, e.g. a
#   subdomain pointing at *.myshopify.com, *.vercel.app, *.herokuapp.com,
#   *.github.io, *.cloudfront.net, or SaaS dashboards (Stripe, SendGrid,
#   Mailgun, status pages). You don't own that stack - do not test it.
#   NOTE: *.caporia.co above WILL match such a subdomain by name, so if one
#   exists, remove the wildcard and list only the hosts you control.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
#  RULES OF ENGAGEMENT   (notes - you enforce these, not the file)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# - Authorized testing only. You own caporia.co and approve this scope.
# - No denial-of-service or stress testing; no social engineering; no physical.
# - Test only your own accounts and data; never pivot to third parties.
# - Passive OSINT (Shodan, exploit search) sends nothing to the target and
#   needs no scope; active modules (portscan / nmap / nuclei) are gated to
#   the IN SCOPE entries above.
